Topic: queue
Subtopic: array, circular array, and linked list implementations
Tier: 2
Source: GFG
Section: Operations on Queue
Subsection: Enqueue (Insert)

Add element at the end of the queue if space is available; otherwise, it results in an Overflow condition.
Time: O(1) , Space: O(1)

```cpp
//C++
void enqueue(int x) {
    if (size == capacity) {
        cout << "Queue Overflow" << endl;
        return;
    }

    arr[size++] = x;
}
```

```c
//C
void enqueue(int x) {
    if (*size == capacity) {
        printf("Queue Overflow");
        return;
    }

    arr[*size] = x;
    (*size)++;
}
```

```java
//JAVA
void enqueue(int x) {
    if (size == capacity) {
        System.out.println("Queue Overflow");
        return;
    }
    arr[size++] = x;
}
```

```python
//PYTHON
